## 2. How ingest works

  Preferred install:

    ./bin/ooda ingest --from fixtures/pm_launch_exec

  Same rail as `qa/pm_ingest_spine.oo`.
  `ooda ingest` reads `DIR/manifest`.
  It slurps `payload`, hashes the bytes, and checks `sha256`.
  It checks name, origin, license, yank, and cap subset of `ooda.pkg`.
  It writes the blob to `.ooda_modules/cas/<sha>/runme.oo`.
  It writes wrapper `ingest_runme.oo` beside that leaf.
  It appends lock v2: `runme@1.0.0#<sha>#FsRead`.
  Success text: `ooda ingest: installed runme cas=`.

  `ooda add` is the named-vendor rail.
  Default vendor is `../registry`.
  `add hello --vendor ../registry` resolves the catalog.
  `add --from DIR` can set the vendor to that dir and take `name` from its manifest.
  Add still walks index, sig, and resolve. It is not the recipe ingest path.
  The smoke uses ingest. It does not use add.

## 3. Smoke

  Path: `scripts/pm_launch_exec_smoke.oo`
  Drive: `./bin/ooda` from the worktree cwd.
  Fail if `bin/ooda` is missing.
  Each child sets `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR=$PWD`.

  Beats:

    1. `./bin/ooda ingest --from fixtures/pm_launch_exec`
       Needle: `ooda ingest: installed runme cas=`
    2. `./bin/ooda launch runme` without `--exec`
       Needle: `ooda launch: ok`
       Must not contain `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`
    3. `./bin/ooda launch --exec runme`
       Must contain `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`
    4. `./bin/ooda launch --exec nosuchpkg`
       Non-zero. Needle: `not installed`
       No `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`. No `ooda launch: ok`

  After `--exec`, `oodac run` may write `runme.oo.bin` next to the CAS leaf.
  The smoke deletes `cas/*/*.bin` and `cas/*/*.tmp.c`.
  Last line: `pm_launch_exec_smoke: PASSED`

